text:
The vishalakshi command runs vault methods from a shell, for example vishalakshi grab https://example.com/post or vishalakshi ask "why does late chunking help". CMDS lists the methods it offers. cmd turns each method into a subcommand. It builds the arguments of the subcommand from the signature of the method. vishalakshi search --help shows the same parameters and descriptions as the documentation. cmd leaves out arguments that cannot be typed on a command line. These are **kwargs, the stop and progress callbacks, stand-in chats and parameters with a callable default. Every command opens the same vault. That vault is the file that $VISHALAKSHI_VAULT names, or ~/.vishalakshi/vault.db when the variable is not set. $VISHALAKSHI_OFFLINE stops the vault from downloading a model. A result is printed as JSON. An answer is printed as prose with its citations.
